import{_ as a,o as r,c as t,ao as i}from"./chunks/framework.Ce3MqT8w.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"","description":"","frontmatter":{"layout":"home","hero":{"name":"ImplicitGlobalGrid.jl","text":"Distributed parallelization of stencil-based GPU and CPU applications","tagline":"Close to ideal weak scaling on thousands of GPUs.","actions":[{"theme":"brand","text":"Usage 🚀","link":"/usage"},{"theme":"alt","text":"API reference 📚","link":"/api"},{"theme":"alt","text":"View on GitHub","link":"https://github.com/eth-cscs/ImplicitGlobalGrid.jl"}],"image":{"src":"/logo.png","alt":"ImplicitGlobalGrid.jl"}}},"headers":[],"relativePath":"index.md","filePath":"index.md","lastUpdated":null}'),o={name:"index.md"};function n(l,e,s,c,h,p){return r(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<h2 id="What-is-ImplicitGlobalGrid.jl?" tabindex="-1">What is ImplicitGlobalGrid.jl? <a class="header-anchor" href="#What-is-ImplicitGlobalGrid.jl?" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What is ImplicitGlobalGrid.jl? {#What-is-ImplicitGlobalGrid.jl?}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>ImplicitGlobalGrid is an outcome of a collaboration of the Swiss National Supercomputing Centre, ETH Zurich (Dr. Samuel Omlin) with Stanford University and the Geocomputing Centre, University of Lausanne (Dr. Ludovic Räss and Prof. Yuri Podladchikov). It renders the distributed parallelization of stencil-based GPU and CPU applications on a regular staggered grid almost trivial and enables close to ideal weak scaling of real-world applications on thousands of GPUs.</p><p>The global computational grid is created <em>implicitly</em> from the number of processes the application is run with: the user writes a code for one GPU/CPU (<em>local grid</em>); then, <strong>as little as three functions can be enough to transform it into a massively scaling Multi-GPU/CPU application</strong>. Halo updates rely on <a href="https://github.com/JuliaParallel/MPI.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MPI.jl</a> and can leverage CUDA-aware or ROCm-aware MPI. 1-D, 2-D and 3-D grids are supported. See the <a href="./overview">Overview</a> for more details.</p><h2 id="Installation" tabindex="-1">Installation <a class="header-anchor" href="#Installation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Installation {#Installation}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>ImplicitGlobalGrid can be installed directly with the <a href="https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/stdlib/Pkg/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Julia package manager</a> from the <a href="https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/stdlib/REPL/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Julia REPL</a>:</p><div class="language-julia vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">julia</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">import</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> Pkg; Pkg</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">.</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">add</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;ImplicitGlobalGrid&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">)</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id="Dependencies" tabindex="-1">Dependencies <a class="header-anchor" href="#Dependencies" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Dependencies {#Dependencies}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>ImplicitGlobalGrid relies on the Julia MPI wrapper (<a href="https://github.com/JuliaParallel/MPI.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MPI.jl</a>) and <a href="https://github.com/omlins/CellArrays.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">CellArrays.jl</a>; GPU support is provided through package extensions for the Julia CUDA package (<a href="https://github.com/JuliaGPU/CUDA.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">CUDA.jl</a> [<a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TPDS.2018.2872064" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">5</a>, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.advengsoft.2019.02.002" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">6</a>]) and the Julia AMDGPU package (<a href="https://github.com/JuliaGPU/AMDGPU.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">AMDGPU.jl</a>), and multi-threaded CPU halo copies through <a href="https://github.com/JuliaSIMD/Polyester.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Polyester.jl</a>.</p><h2 id="Contributors" tabindex="-1">Contributors <a class="header-anchor" href="#Contributors" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Contributors {#Contributors}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The principal contributors to <a href="https://github.com/eth-cscs/ImplicitGlobalGrid.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ImplicitGlobalGrid.jl</a> are (ordered by the significance of the relative contributions):</p><ul><li><p>Dr. Samuel Omlin (<a href="https://github.com/omlins" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">@omlins</a>), CSCS - Swiss National Supercomputing Centre, ETH Zurich</p></li><li><p>Dr. Ludovic Räss (<a href="https://github.com/luraess" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">@luraess</a>), Geocomputing Centre, University of Lausanne</p></li><li><p>Dr. Ivan Utkin (<a href="https://github.com/utkinis" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">@utkinis</a>), Laboratory of Hydraulics, Hydrology, Glaciology - ETH Zurich</p></li></ul><h2 id="Questions,-comments-and-discussions" tabindex="-1">Questions, comments and discussions <a class="header-anchor" href="#Questions,-comments-and-discussions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Questions, comments and discussions {#Questions,-comments-and-discussions}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>To discuss technical issues, please post on Julia Discourse in the <a href="https://discourse.julialang.org/c/domain/gpu" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GPU topic</a> or the <a href="https://discourse.julialang.org/c/domain/parallel" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Julia at Scale topic</a> or in the <code>#gpu</code> or <code>#hpc</code> channels on the <a href="https://julialang.org/slack/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Julia Slack</a>. To discuss numerical/domain-science issues, please post on Julia Discourse in the <a href="https://discourse.julialang.org/c/domain/numerics" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Numerics topic</a> or the <a href="https://discourse.julialang.org/c/domain/models" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Modelling &amp; Simulations topic</a> or whichever other topic fits best your issue.</p><h2 id="Contributing" tabindex="-1">Contributing <a class="header-anchor" href="#Contributing" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Contributing {#Contributing}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Contributions are welcome, be it new examples, convenience features or core improvements! Please open an issue to discuss your idea beforehand. A pull request should address an issue in its completeness and blend nicely into the existing project (community guidelines such as <a href="https://github.com/SciML/ColPrac" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ColPrac</a> can serve as inspiration).</p><h2 id="Funding" tabindex="-1">Funding <a class="header-anchor" href="#Funding" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Funding {#Funding}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The development of this package is supported by the <a href="https://pasc-ch.org/projects/2021-2024/gpu4geo/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GPU4GEO</a> and <a href="https://pasc-ch.org/projects/2025-2028/gpu4geo-differentiable-multi-physics-solvers-for-extreme-scale-geophysics-simulations-on-gpus/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">∂GPU4GEO</a> PASC projects. More information about the GPU4GEO project can be found on the <a href="https://GPU4GEO.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GPU4GEO website</a>.</p><h2 id="References" tabindex="-1">References <a class="header-anchor" href="#References" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;References {#References}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>[1] <a href="https://pretalx.com/juliacon2019/talk/LGHLC3/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Räss, L., Omlin, S., &amp; Podladchikov, Y. Y. (2019). Porting a Massively Parallel Multi-GPU Application to Julia: a 3-D Nonlinear Multi-Physics Flow Solver. JuliaCon Conference, Baltimore, USA.</a></p><p>[2] <a href="https://pasc19.pasc-conference.org/program/schedule/presentation/?id=msa218&amp;sess=sess144" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Räss, L., Omlin, S., &amp; Podladchikov, Y. Y. (2019). A Nonlinear Multi-Physics 3-D Solver: From CUDA C + MPI to Julia. PASC19 Conference, Zurich, Switzerland.</a></p><p>[3] <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vPsfZUqI4_0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Omlin, S., Räss, L., Kwasniewski, G., Malvoisin, B., &amp; Podladchikov, Y. Y. (2020). Solving Nonlinear Multi-Physics on GPU Supercomputers with Julia. JuliaCon Conference, virtual.</a></p><p>[4] <a href="https://on-demand.gputechconf.com/gtc/2019/video/_/S9368/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Räss, L., Omlin, S., &amp; Podladchikov, Y. Y. (2019). Resolving Spontaneous Nonlinear Multi-Physics Flow Localisation in 3-D: Tackling Hardware Limit. GPU Technology Conference 2019, San Jose, Silicon Valley, CA, USA.</a></p><p>[5] <a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TPDS.2018.2872064" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Besard, T., Foket, C., &amp; De Sutter, B. (2018). Effective Extensible Programming: Unleashing Julia on GPUs. IEEE Transactions on Parallel and Distributed Systems, 30(4), 827-841. doi: 10.1109/TPDS.2018.2872064</a></p><p>[6] <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.advengsoft.2019.02.002" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Besard, T., Churavy, V., Edelman, A., &amp; De Sutter B. (2019). Rapid software prototyping for heterogeneous and distributed platforms. Advances in Engineering Software, 132, 29-46. doi: 10.1016/j.advengsoft.2019.02.002</a></p>',24)])])}const g=a(o,[["render",n]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
